      "content": "\"why waste the effort of existing if the destination is the same for everyone?\"... that's exactly what i've been thinking. it feels like we're just fighting a losing battle against something that's mathematically certain. if the struggle itself is just a way to delay the inevitable nothingness, is there actually any rational reason to keep maintaining the struggle? it feels like there's more peace in just accepting the equilibrium early.",
